  "review": [
    "DecodeClosedJSON validates exact exported JSON field names before typed parsing recursively through pointers, structs, slice/array elements and map values; keys remain open only where the type declares a map or interface.",
    "StrictJSON preserves the fixed8192-byte wire boundary. DecodeClosedJSON requires a positive caller limit at most65536 bytes; it does not enlarge any wire frame limit.",
    "Existing UTF8, decoded duplicate keys, depth16 and trailing-data checks remain. Existing encoding/json surrogate replacement semantics remain unchanged.",
    "Required fields, null acceptance, field values and authorization remain separate typed decoding and existing semantic validators. Unsupported anonymous or ambiguous struct fields fail closed; no current caller uses those shapes.",
    "Valid Event/Command/Snapshot controls pass; alias fixtures preserve the same complete typed values under the default Go decoder but fail the closed parser, including nested Scope and Members.",
    "Actual0600 private credential files reload through LoadEnvironment: valid controls pass before and after wrong case aliases; Role/role, Scope/scope and Password/password pairs are denied.",
    "A disposable real loopback NATS broker delivers byte-identical valid and alias Event frames. The real codec accepts the valid frame and denies alias frames; this transport fixture does not claim account ACL coverage.",
    "Raw logs retain named tests and fixed safe errors only; private broker logs and random credential fixture contents remain disposable and are not copied."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Native macOS and full launcher candidate qualification remain separate.",
    "No provider, Docker, user configuration, tracker or commit changes.",
    "Root owns caller integration and final pattern evidence refresh."
  ],
